WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:18.074
Joy woke up to the smell of pancakes.

2
00:00:18.075 --> 00:00:21.420
"Mom is making pancakes?" she thought.

3
00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.443
That was unusual.

4
00:00:23.444 --> 00:00:26.349
Joy rushed downstairs.

5
00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:29.095
"Grandpa!" she cried.

6
00:00:29.096 --> 00:00:33.112
Grandpa was in front of the stove, flipping pancakes.

7
00:00:33.113 --> 00:00:36.421
"Who wants pancakes?" he asked.

8
00:00:36.422 --> 00:00:39.891
Joy gave her grandfather a huge hug.

9
00:00:39.892 --> 00:00:42.011
"When did you get back?"

10
00:00:42.012 --> 00:00:43.252
"Early this morning.

11
00:00:43.253 --> 00:00:47.828
Your dad and I woke up at sunrise and drove straight here," he said.

12
00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:51.124
"I heard you were up late, finishing schoolwork."

13
00:00:51.125 --> 00:00:56.425
Joy grinned. "I was. But I finished my leaders project.

14
00:00:56.426 --> 00:01:00.417
So I'm ready for pancakes and ready to play in the snow!"

15
00:01:00.418 --> 00:01:03.782
Just then Katie bounced into the kitchen.

16
00:01:03.783 --> 00:01:08.735
At the same time, Dad came in the backdoor, carrying firewood.

17
00:01:08.736 --> 00:01:10.961
Mom followed him.

18
00:01:10.962 --> 00:01:15.754
"Dad! Grandpa!" Katie cried, surprised.

19
00:01:15.755 --> 00:01:19.874
"I can't wait to hear all about your weekend," Dad said.

20
00:01:19.875 --> 00:01:25.080
He gave Katie's ponytail a playful tug.

21
00:01:25.081 --> 00:01:29.679
"Isn't it nice that we're all home together again?" Mom said.

22
00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:34.267
Grandpa set a huge stack of pancakes on the table.

23
00:01:34.268 --> 00:01:42.117
"And isn't it nice that Grandpa is back to cook breakfast for us?" Katie replied. Mom laughed.

24
00:01:42.118 --> 00:01:46.196
"So what did we miss while we were away?" Grandpa asked.

25
00:01:46.197 --> 00:01:48.135
He winked at Mom.

26
00:01:48.136 --> 00:01:52.057
"Besides cold cereal and burnt brownies?"

27
00:01:52.058 --> 00:01:57.757
"Well, first of all, it was freezing outside," Katie began.

28
00:01:57.758 --> 00:02:01.975
"And we thought we had an egg and chicken thief!" Joy added.

29
00:02:01.976 --> 00:02:06.037
"But really some chickens were escaping through a hole in the fence!

30
00:02:06.038 --> 00:02:11.429
And they were laying eggs in your burn pile, Grandpa," Katie said.

31
00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:14.952
"Wow!" said Grandpa, surprised.

32
00:02:14.953 --> 00:02:18.418
"I'm glad there wasn't a real thief!" said Dad.

33
00:02:18.419 --> 00:02:26.306
"Then Joy fixed the hole in the fence all by herself," Katie said with her mouth full of pancakes.

34
00:02:26.307 --> 00:02:29.300
"Wonderful!" said Grandpa.

35
00:02:29.301 --> 00:02:34.847
"And tomorrow at school we're finally giving our reports on leaders," said Joy.

36
00:02:34.848 --> 00:02:38.907
"Who did you end up choosing, Joy?" Grandpa asked.

37
00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:41.849
"Harriet Tubman," Joy said.

38
00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:45.271
"She spent her whole life working for something important:

39
00:02:45.272 --> 00:02:47.594
getting slaves to freedom."

40
00:02:47.595 --> 00:02:50.284
"Good choice," said Dad.

41
00:02:50.285 --> 00:02:56.242
"Thanks." Joy poured maple syrup on her pancakes, thinking for a minute.

42
00:02:56.243 --> 00:03:00.585
Would she ever be a great leader like Harriet Tubman?

43
00:03:00.586 --> 00:03:03.248
"Dad," Joy said slowly.

44
00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:07.198
"When you were a kid, what did you want to be when you grew up?"

45
00:03:07.199 --> 00:03:12.238
Dad smiled. "I wanted to work in a park, taking care of trees."

46
00:03:12.239 --> 00:03:17.475
"Now you take care of trees by helping people recycle!" Katie said.

47
00:03:17.476 --> 00:03:21.137
Dad laughed. "I guess I do."

48
00:03:21.138 --> 00:03:24.367
"What about you, Grandpa?" asked Katie.

49
00:03:24.368 --> 00:03:28.944
Grandpa had been a mailman in Willow Creek for thirty years.

50
00:03:28.945 --> 00:03:34.433
"I knew I wanted to be a mailman since I was nine years old," Grandpa said.

51
00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:39.334
"I loved seeing people smile when they got a special letter or package."

52
00:03:39.335 --> 00:03:43.614
"I always wanted to be a librarian," Mom chimed in.

53
00:03:43.615 --> 00:03:45.722
"What about you girls?"

54
00:03:45.723 --> 00:03:50.279
"I'm going to be the mayor of Willow Creek!" Katie announced.

55
00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:53.651
Dad laughed. "That's perfect for you."

56
00:03:53.652 --> 00:03:56.546
Joy grinned from ear to ear.

57
00:03:56.547 --> 00:03:59.621
"I want to be a vet," she said.

58
00:03:59.622 --> 00:04:03.317
"Those are great jobs," Grandpa said.

59
00:04:03.318 --> 00:04:06.422
"They're about helping others, just like leaders do.

60
00:04:06.423 --> 00:04:08.692
And like sisters do too."

61
00:04:08.693 --> 00:04:11.676
The twins smiled at each other.

62
00:04:11.677 --> 00:04:14.165
"So, sister," Katie said.

63
00:04:14.166 --> 00:04:16.990
"Are you done with your pancakes yet?"

64
00:04:16.991 --> 00:04:20.478
"Yep. I'm done," Joy told her twin.

65
00:04:20.479 --> 00:04:24.290
"Time to go play in the snow!"

66
00:04:24.291 --> 00:04:26.808
Katie was already by the door.

67
00:04:26.809 --> 00:04:31.063
"Catch!" she said, tossing Joy's boots at her.

68
00:04:31.064 --> 00:04:34.034
Joy laughed as she caught the boots.

69
00:04:34.035 --> 00:04:37.815
Sometimes she wished she had an older sister.

70
00:04:37.816 --> 00:04:41.394
Other times she wished she had a younger sister.

71
00:04:41.395 --> 00:04:46.977
But today she was glad that she and Katie were twins.

72
00:04:46.978 --> 00:04:50.982
"Isn't it fun being a twin sister?" Joy asked.

73
00:04:50.983 --> 00:04:53.871
"Yes," answered Katie.

74
00:04:53.872 --> 00:04:58.462
"Sometimes it's even fun being your twin sister!"

75
00:04:58.463 --> 00:05:05.455
Then the Willow Creek twins raced out into the snow together.
